{:edb/db-before-t 2573 :edb/db-after-t 2574 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535886 50 #inst "2026-10-09T09:55:02.434Z" 13194139535886 true] [17592186175904 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372643 13194139535886 true] [17592186175921 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372615 13194139535886 true] [17592186175921 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372622 13194139535886 true] [17592186175991 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372629 13194139535886 true] [17592186175991 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372636 13194139535886 true] [17592186372615 1017 #edb/ref 17592186372616 13194139535886 true] [17592186372615 1089 "q-161140" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372615 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535886 true] [17592186372615 1100 "Consider the portion of the surface $z=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+y$ whose projection onto the $xy$-plane is bounded by the curve $y=\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}},$ and the $x$-axis. Find a repeated integral expression for the surface area of this surface." 13194139535886 true] [17592186372615 1113 #uuid "c80d473c-0162-5abc-8ee1-574a19c892a1" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372615 1145 "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=f(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\nz=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+y,\\,(x,y)\\in D\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071034/assets/8bf7a5921936b44a2e672fcee524c5a230800e6130f6c0a8683e6ce46829df58.png)\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+y)=1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{2}+(1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{2+{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\sqrt{2+{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372616 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372617 13194139535886 true] [17592186372616 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372618 13194139535886 true] [17592186372616 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372619 13194139535886 true] [17592186372616 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372620 13194139535886 true] [17592186372616 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372621 13194139535886 true] [17592186372616 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535886 true] [17592186372616 1041 "selection" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372616 1104 #edb/ref 17592186372617 13194139535886 true] [17592186372616 1110 #uuid "d9408cd7-d550-5d66-9ec9-1b71a3b46056" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372617 1034 "{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\sqrt{2+{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372617 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535886 true] [17592186372617 1111 #uuid "297c340e-5e01-5015-850f-a8076023f086" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372618 1034 "{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\sqrt{2+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372618 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535886 true] [17592186372618 1111 #uuid "2ede9c81-0910-5081-ad94-d8b5ccb9e337" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372619 1034 "{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\sqrt{1+4{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372619 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535886 true] [17592186372619 1111 #uuid "d084eae4-e165-5148-a0c2-713018d19404" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372620 1034 "{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+y}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372620 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535886 true] [17592186372620 1111 #uuid "150bc16a-c6c1-56c3-bc18-28f9de01414d" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372621 1034 "{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\sqrt{1+{sin}^{2}⁡x+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372621 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535886 true] [17592186372621 1111 #uuid "70e34ca7-e1ca-58e3-b5a9-67567856228c" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372622 1017 #edb/ref 17592186372623 13194139535886 true] [17592186372622 1089 "q-161141" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372622 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535886 true] [17592186372622 1100 "Consider the portion of the surface $z=y{e}^{x}$ whose projection onto the $xy$-plane is bounded by the lines $y=2x,$ $x=1,$ and the $x$-axis. Find a repeated integral expression for the surface area of this surface." 13194139535886 true] [17592186372622 1113 #uuid "dc263672-04e3-59a9-9f18-ccb933eb5e00" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372622 1145 "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=f(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\nz=y{e}^{x},\\,(x,y)\\in D\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2x},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071034/assets/903b7f3c6bd9721a974160487ca5099fdf54ce02b61697a7830bb662b26d8953.png)\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y{e}^{x})=y{e}^{x}, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{e}^{x})={e}^{x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+(y{e}^{x})^{2}+({e}^{x})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+({y}^{2}+1){e}^{2x}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}\\sqrt{1+({y}^{2}+1){e}^{2x}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372623 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372624 13194139535886 true] [17592186372623 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372625 13194139535886 true] [17592186372623 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372626 13194139535886 true] [17592186372623 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372627 13194139535886 true] [17592186372623 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372628 13194139535886 true] [17592186372623 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535886 true] [17592186372623 1041 "selection" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372623 1104 #edb/ref 17592186372626 13194139535886 true] [17592186372623 1110 #uuid "b1c6921d-b4c3-59eb-a40d-7b38753d0c1a" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372624 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}\\sqrt{1+(y+1){e}^{x}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372624 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535886 true] [17592186372624 1111 #uuid "faa9d216-af54-561c-9356-f57d7270d690" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372625 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}\\sqrt{1+(y+1){e}^{2x}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372625 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535886 true] [17592186372625 1111 #uuid "4e357698-49e7-5b00-9576-1d3dd1590c42" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372626 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}\\sqrt{1+({y}^{2}+1){e}^{2x}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372626 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535886 true] [17592186372626 1111 #uuid "8d9cfb6b-c5c2-5b04-afce-222dd48d0756" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372627 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}\\sqrt{1+({y}^{2}+1){e}^{x}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372627 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535886 true] [17592186372627 1111 #uuid "bf62a55b-aba0-574a-9d39-49eaddb798ad" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372628 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}1+{y}^{2}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372628 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535886 true] [17592186372628 1111 #uuid "c6f7c504-b323-544e-bcf8-407870bdad30" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372629 1017 #edb/ref 17592186372630 13194139535886 true] [17592186372629 1089 "q-161173" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372629 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535886 true] [17592186372629 1100 "Find the surface area of the part of the hyperbolic paraboloid $x={z}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ that is subject to the constraints ${y}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\le 9$ and $z\\le 0.$" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372629 1113 #uuid "a6ee91a7-8625-5e8e-b323-bf06c3b28986" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372629 1145 "For a surface $S$ defined by $x=f(y,z)$ with $(y,z)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂x}{∂y})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂x}{∂z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\nx={z}^{2}-{y}^{2},\\,(y,z)\\in D\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\le 9,\\,z\\le 0},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071034/assets/cd5bcd7857769afb5f3a4f6197757c08eb295c7075a271c302c4b6087d661d14.png)\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({z}^{2}-{y}^{2})=-2y, \\\\ \\frac{∂x}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({z}^{2}-{y}^{2})=2z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂x}{∂y})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂x}{∂z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+(-2y)^{2}+(2z)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+4{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+4({y}^{2}+{z}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region $D$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 3,\\,\\pi \\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula for polar coordinates, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+4({y}^{2}+{z}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}\\sqrt{1+4{r}^{2}}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{3}r\\sqrt{1+4{r}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta {\\int }_{0}^{3}r\\sqrt{1+4{r}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}r \\\\  & =\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{3}r\\sqrt{1+4{r}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}r.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $u=1+4{r}^{2},$ we get $\\text{d}u=8r\\,\\text{d}r.$ Also, the limits must be changed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & 0 & 3 \\\\ u & 1 & 37\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSubstituting these into our integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{3}r\\sqrt{1+4{r}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}r & =\\pi \\cdot \\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{1}^{37}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{8}{\\int }_{1}^{37}{u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}{[{u}^{3/2}]}_{1}^{37} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}{[{u}^{3/2}]}_{1}^{37} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}[(37)^{3/2}-1] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi (37\\sqrt{37}-1)}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372630 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372631 13194139535886 true] [17592186372630 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372632 13194139535886 true] [17592186372630 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372633 13194139535886 true] [17592186372630 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372634 13194139535886 true] [17592186372630 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372635 13194139535886 true] [17592186372630 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535886 true] [17592186372630 1041 "selection" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372630 1104 #edb/ref 17592186372631 13194139535886 true] [17592186372630 1110 #uuid "1f530898-ab7e-59bb-8eef-3c68c3406203" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372631 1034 "\\frac{\\pi (37\\sqrt{37}-1)}{12}" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372631 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535886 true] [17592186372631 1111 #uuid "d76cb245-e7df-549b-a063-88c05ab13f9f" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372632 1034 "\\frac{\\pi (\\sqrt{37}-1)}{6}" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372632 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535886 true] [17592186372632 1111 #uuid "d963bf1e-30b5-5613-8985-be316360be9c" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372633 1034 "\\pi (3\\sqrt{15}-1)" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372633 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535886 true] [17592186372633 1111 #uuid "6372fa17-961b-5d7a-81da-1f823c644bb5" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372634 1034 "\\frac{\\pi (17\\sqrt{15}-1)}{6}" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372634 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535886 true] [17592186372634 1111 #uuid "896b79af-1e73-5ad1-96f0-1a29ef3f9f93" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372635 1034 "2\\pi (\\sqrt{23}-1)" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372635 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535886 true] [17592186372635 1111 #uuid "85c9aa58-62ce-5825-b76f-68ac2a6e3046" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372636 1017 #edb/ref 17592186372637 13194139535886 true] [17592186372636 1089 "q-161174" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372636 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535886 true] [17592186372636 1100 "Find the surface area of the part of the plane $x=2-y-z$ that is subject to the constraints ${y}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\le 1$ and $y\\ge 0,\\,z\\ge 0.$" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372636 1113 #uuid "e5656941-1309-55ef-a6db-4d55ea948859" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372636 1145 "For a surface $S$ defined by $x=f(y,z)$ with $(y,z)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂x}{∂y})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂x}{∂z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\nx=2-y-z,\\,(y,z)\\in D\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\le 1,\\,y\\ge 0,\\,z\\ge 0},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071034/assets/3741c5db05232f04f60f747dc04176bfc77da30bbc39c79888cf4c18939369f7.png)\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2-y-z)=-1, \\\\ \\frac{∂x}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2-y-z)=-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂x}{∂y})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂x}{∂z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+1+1}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region $D$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 1,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula for polar coordinates, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}\\sqrt{3}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta {\\int }_{0}^{1}r\\,\\text{d}r \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\cdot [\\theta ]_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\cdot {[\\frac{{r}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi \\sqrt{3}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372637 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372638 13194139535886 true] [17592186372637 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372639 13194139535886 true] [17592186372637 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372640 13194139535886 true] [17592186372637 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372641 13194139535886 true] [17592186372637 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372642 13194139535886 true] [17592186372637 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535886 true] [17592186372637 1041 "selection" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372637 1104 #edb/ref 17592186372639 13194139535886 true] [17592186372637 1110 #uuid "9e65377f-79e0-5dd6-88e3-e44727b6dc9d" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372638 1034 "\\frac{\\pi (\\sqrt{3}+1)}{4}" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372638 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535886 true] [17592186372638 1111 #uuid "500e43be-8a93-5b22-aaaf-d02ba9fd34a7" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372639 1034 "\\frac{\\pi \\sqrt{3}}{4}" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372639 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535886 true] [17592186372639 1111 #uuid "ceda287a-8ac4-5665-9018-863a083d4207" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372640 1034 "3\\pi \\sqrt{2}" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372640 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535886 true] [17592186372640 1111 #uuid "86828f55-be93-54b2-a69f-40b4ad8dc3d8" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372641 1034 "\\frac{\\pi \\sqrt{2}}{3}" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372641 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535886 true] [17592186372641 1111 #uuid "8ceca33d-e4c0-55c9-af8a-5a1b58f12e46" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372642 1034 "2\\pi \\sqrt{3}" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372642 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535886 true] [17592186372642 1111 #uuid "49dc6f8c-084c-579e-b8d0-9244ba3c7165" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372643 1017 #edb/ref 17592186372644 13194139535886 true] [17592186372643 1089 "q-161177" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372643 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535886 true] [17592186372643 1100 "Find the surface area of the part of the surface $y=\\frac{4}{7}{x}^{7/4}+z$ whose projection onto the $xz$-plane is bounded by $z=\\sqrt{x},$ $x=4,$ and the $x$-axis." 13194139535886 true] [17592186372643 1113 #uuid "fd88a418-4002-5970-8160-0236976b62b8" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372643 1145 "For a surface $S$ defined by $y=f(x,z)$ with $(x,z)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{4}{7}{x}^{7/4}+z,\\,(x,z)\\in D,\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 4,\\,0\\le z\\le \\sqrt{x}},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071034/assets/0a4ed826b683e7e8d8ed3e05bcb75618e74314febcdda8ae31b09f379ca21c73.png)\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂y}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{4}{7}{x}^{7/4}+z)={x}^{3/4}, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\frac{4}{7}{x}^{7/4}+z)=1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{({x}^{3/4})}^{2}+(1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{2+{x}^{3/2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}\\sqrt{2+{x}^{3/2}}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\sqrt{2+{x}^{3/2}}\\cdot z\\,{|}_{z=0}^{z=\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\sqrt{2+{x}^{3/2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $u=2+{x}^{3/2},$ we get $\\text{d}u=\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Also, the limits must be changed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & 0 & 4 \\\\ u & 2 & 10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSubstituting these into our integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\sqrt{2+{x}^{3/2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{2}^{10}\\frac{2}{3}{u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}{u}^{3/2}\\,{|}_{2}^{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}({10}^{3/2}-{2}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}(10\\sqrt{10}-2\\sqrt{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\sqrt{2}}{9}(5\\sqrt{5}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372644 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372645 13194139535886 true] [17592186372644 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372646 13194139535886 true] [17592186372644 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372647 13194139535886 true] [17592186372644 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372648 13194139535886 true] [17592186372644 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372649 13194139535886 true] [17592186372644 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535886 true] [17592186372644 1041 "selection" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372644 1104 #edb/ref 17592186372649 13194139535886 true] [17592186372644 1110 #uuid "75f34f71-fb75-5a90-b1b1-e3c85d832aad" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372645 1034 "2(5\\sqrt{5}-1)" 13194139535886 true] [17592186372645 1103 #edb/ref 1759